7: ### Key Components\n\n  Line 64: ### Data Flow\n\n  Line 67: ### Head Form\n\n  Line 85: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n  Line 105: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\n  Line 113: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n  Line 125: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n  Line 140: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n  Line 149: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n  Line 165: ## DECISIONS ALREADY MADE\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md\",\"pattern\":\"^## |^### \"}"},"time":{"start":1794527700864,"end":1794527702126}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794527704732,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","part":{"id":"prt_1d22fb69c001oONUvDi4yfhmYV","sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","messageID":"msg_1d22f9c0e0018Rz0e3EomNHu73","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"d30582cf0aeb5992492de1285b5a7bb6a2107773","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":7082,"output":228,"reasoning":85,"cache":{"read":16768,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794527706900,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","part":{"id":"prt_1d22fbf13001y65SMeFO0279up","sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","messageID":"msg_1d22fb6a10010LnUs4VDV3y2rg","type":"step-start","snapshot":"cce5217044ab7a1a4f54e2edd25bd2e8380117fd"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794527706932,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","part":{"partID":"prt_1d22fbf15001J1gadHFgTSjyF4","sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","messageID":"msg_1d22fb6a10010LnUs4VDV3y2rg","type":"tool","id":"call_e7f7fa14d713460e91d0d229","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md","offset":50,"limit":60},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md, lines 50-109\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n52: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n53: \n54: ### Pattern\n55: One generated table, many readers. Nothing hand-keeps a command string or a policy.\n56: \n57: ### Key Components\n58: - **Command table** (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, generated by `derive-command-bridges.cjs`): `COMMAND_ROWS` maps every id a scorer can return for a command entry, the TypeScript id, the Python id and the inventory id, to `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }`. `COMMAND_POLICIES` maps each runnable string to its policy. Without it each reader would rebuild the join from `commandPolicies`, the doctor details and the projection.\n59: - **Public fields** (`ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): `publicRecommendation` copies `kind` and, for a row found in `COMMAND_ROWS`, sets `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. `enrichCompiledRoutes` adds the policy of an attached command and reads the already-offered set from the `command` fields instead of from bridge keywords.\n60: - **Brief head** (`ADV/lib/render.ts`): a recommendation with a command renders `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`, where the owner is `ownerSkillId` or, for a hub with an attached command, the hub id. Fields win, and `COMMAND_ROWS` fills a missing field by id, which covers an older daemon and the Python subprocess path.\n61: - **Degraded contract** (`ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`): `degradedRecommendations` keeps a command row's fields only when its bare slash command appears in the prompt, and otherwise replaces it with its owner skill.\n62: - **Reach check** (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`): `rankShippedFleet` counts a hit when the first shipped entry is the hub or is a command row whose `ownerSkillId` is the hub.\n63: \n64: ### Data Flow\n65: `command-metadata.json`, `_routes.yaml` and the projection feed the deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n66: \n67: ### Head Form\n68: The six golden heads, one per family, each followed by the existing `\\nDirectives:` block:\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.\n72: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask) 0.82/0.16 pass.\n73: Advisor: live; use sk-design → /design:chart (start) 0.90/0.12 pass.\n74: Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.\n75: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n76: Advisor: live; use sk-prompt → /prompt:improve (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n77: ```\n78: \n79: The policies come from `commandPolicies` today. A recommendation with no command keeps today's `use <skill>` head. A command row with no table entry keeps its sanitized id. A missing policy drops the parenthesis.\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n85: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n86: \n87: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n88: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n89: | `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` and `renderDoctorCommandStrings` | Doctor-only runnable labels | Replace with `COMMAND_ROWS`, keep `doctorCommandString` as a wrapper | `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS\"` prints nothing and the doctor tests pass |\n90: | `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` | Already-offered set from bridge keywords | Read the `command` fields instead | `tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` |\n91: | `recommendationFromCli` | Keeps `command` only, forces `kind: 'skill'` | Keep `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` | Hook fallback tests |\n92: | `degradedRecommendations` | Copies skill id and scores | Apply the degraded contract | New degraded test |\n93: | `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94: | `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95: | Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n96: | `AGENTS.md`, Gate 2 and pointers | Phase 006 | Unchanged | `git diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` |\n97: | `Also:` companion line | Doctor-only second command | Unchanged | Doctor brief tests |\n98: \n99: Matrix axes for the renderer: a field present or absent, an id in the table or not, a policy present or absent, ambiguous or not. Every axis has one test row.\n100: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n105: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n106: \n107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n108: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n109: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 110]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md, lines 50-109\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n52: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n53: \n54: ### Pattern\n55: One generated table, many readers. Nothing hand-keeps a command string or a policy.\n56: \n57: ### Key Components\n58: - **Command table** (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, generated by `derive-command-bridges.cjs`): `COMMAND_ROWS` maps every id a scorer can return for a command entry, the TypeScript id, the Python id and the inventory id, to `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }`. `COMMAND_POLICIES` maps each runnable string to its policy. Without it each reader would rebuild the join from `commandPolicies`, the doctor details and the projection.\n59: - **Public fields** (`ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): `publicRecommendation` copies `kind` and, for a row found in `COMMAND_ROWS`, sets `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. `enrichCompiledRoutes` adds the policy of an attached command and reads the already-offered set from the `command` fields instead of from bridge keywords.\n60: - **Brief head** (`ADV/lib/render.ts`): a recommendation with a command renders `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`, where the owner is `ownerSkillId` or, for a hub with an attached command, the hub id. Fields win, and `COMMAND_ROWS` fills a missing field by id, which covers an older daemon and the Python subprocess path.\n61: - **Degraded contract** (`ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`): `degradedRecommendations` keeps a command row's fields only when its bare slash command appears in the prompt, and otherwise replaces it with its owner skill.\n62: - **Reach check** (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`): `rankShippedFleet` counts a hit when the first shipped entry is the hub or is a command row whose `ownerSkillId` is the hub.\n63: \n64: ### Data Flow\n65: `command-metadata.json`, `_routes.yaml` and the projection feed the deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n66: \n67: ### Head Form\n68: The six golden heads, one per family, each followed by the existing `\\nDirectives:` block:\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.\n72: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask) 0.82/0.16 pass.\n73: Advisor: live; use sk-design → /design:chart (start) 0.90/0.12 pass.\n74: Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.\n75: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n76: Advisor: live; use sk-prompt → /prompt:improve (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n77: ```\n78: \n79: The policies come from `commandPolicies` today. A recommendation with no command keeps today's `use <skill>` head. A command row with no table entry keeps its sanitized id. A missing policy drops the parenthesis.\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n85: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n86: \n87: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n88: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n89: | `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` and `renderDoctorCommandStrings` | Doctor-only runnable labels | Replace with `COMMAND_ROWS`, keep `doctorCommandString` as a wrapper | `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS\"` prints nothing and the doctor tests pass |\n90: | `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` | Already-offered set from bridge keywords | Read the `command` fields instead | `tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` |\n91: | `recommendationFromCli` | Keeps `command` only, forces `kind: 'skill'` | Keep `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` | Hook fallback tests |\n92: | `degradedRecommendations` | Copies skill id and scores | Apply the degraded contract | New degraded test |\n93: | `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94: | `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95: | Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n96: | `AGENTS.md`, Gate 2 and pointers | Phase 006 | Unchanged | `git diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` |\n97: | `Also:` companion line | Doctor-only second command | Unchanged | Doctor brief tests |\n98: \n99: Matrix axes for the renderer: a field present or absent, an id in the table or not, a policy present or absent, ambiguous or not. Every axis has one test row.\n100: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n105: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n106: \n107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n108: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n109: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 110]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md\",\"offset\":50,\"limit\":60}"},"time":{"start":1794527706901,"end":1794527706932}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794527706945,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","part":{"partID":"prt_1d22fbf18001lEQYbB1aNfr6px","sessionID":"ses_e2dd11594ffe4d32Avi4cOny22","messageID":"msg_1d22fb6a10010LnUs4VDV3y2rg","type":"tool","id":"call_cd46e3dd41044aedbf969747","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts","offset":140,"limit":120},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts, lines 140-259\n140:   return Math.min(Math.max(1, Math.floor(tokenCap)), MAX_TOKEN_CAP);\n141: }\n142: \n143: function capText(text: string, tokenCap: number): string {\n144:   const charCap = tokenCap * TOKEN_TO_CHAR_ESTIMATE;\n145:   if (text.length <= charCap) {\n146:     return text;\n147:   }\n148:   const truncated = text.slice(0, Math.max(1, charCap - 3)).trimEnd();\n149:   return `${truncated}...`;\n150: }\n151: \n152: function sanitizeSkillLabel(skillLabel: string | null | undefined): string | null {\n153:   if (typeof skillLabel !== 'string') {\n154:     return null;\n155:   }\n156:   const folded = canonicalFold(skillLabel);\n157:   if (/[\\n\\r]/.test(folded)) {\n158:     return null;\n159:   }\n160:   const singleLine = folded\n161:     .replace(CONTROL_CHAR_PATTERN, '')\n162:     .replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')\n163:     .trim();\n164:   if (!singleLine || INSTRUCTION_LABEL_PATTERN.test(singleLine)) {\n165:     return null;\n166:   }\n167:   return singleLine;\n168: }\n169: \n170: const DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX = 'command-doctor-';\n171: \n172: function isDoctorBridgeId(skillId: string): boolean {\n173:   return skillId.startsWith(DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX);\n174: }\n175: \n176: /** Return the sanitized runnable command for a doctor bridge id, or null when unmapped. */\n177: export function doctorCommandString(skillId: string): string | null {\n178:   if (!isDoctorBridgeId(skillId)) {\n179:     return null;\n180:   }\n181:   const command = commandRowFor(skillId)?.command;\n182:   return command === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(command);\n183: }\n184: \n185: // A recommendation that names a command renders as the skill that owns it, the\n186: // runnable command and the policy that governs the run. The recommendation's own\n187: // fields stay authoritative and the generated row fills only what they omit, so a\n188: // caller that already resolved the command is never second-guessed.\n189: function commandLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation): string | null {\n190:   const row = commandRowFor(recommendation.skill);\n191:   const command = recommendation.command ?? row?.command;\n192:   const owner = recommendation.ownerSkillId ?? row?.ownerSkillId ?? recommendation.skill;\n193:   const policy = recommendation.policy ?? row?.policy;\n194:   const commandPart = command === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(command);\n195:   const ownerPart = sanitizeSkillLabel(owner);\n196:   if (!commandPart || !ownerPart) {\n197:     return null;\n198:   }\n199:   const policyPart = policy === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(policy);\n200:   return policyPart === null\n201:     ? `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart}`\n202:     : `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart} (${policyPart})`;\n203: }\n204: \n205: // A doctor bridge renders as its runnable command and never as its raw id; an\n206: // unmapped doctor id renders nothing.\n207: function recommendationLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation): string | null {\n208:   return commandLabel(recommendation)\n209:     ?? (isDoctorBridgeId(recommendation.skill)\n210:       ? doctorCommandString(recommendation.skill)\n211:       : sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill));\n212: }\n213: \n214: function formatScore(value: number): string {\n215:   return Number.isFinite(value) ? value.toFixed(2) : '0.00';\n216: }\n217: \n218: type RenderableRecommendation = AdvisorRecommendation & {\n219:   readonly score?: number;\n220:   readonly ambiguousWith?: readonly string[];\n221:   readonly heldBelow?: string;\n222: };\n223: \n224: function toScoredRecommendation(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation): AdvisorScoredRecommendation {\n225:   return {\n226:     skill: recommendation.skill,\n227:     kind: recommendation.kind === 'command' ? 'command' : 'skill',\n228:     confidence: recommendation.confidence,\n229:     uncertainty: recommendation.uncertainty,\n230:     passes_threshold: recommendation.passes_threshold ?? true,\n231:     reason: '',\n232:     score: typeof recommendation.score === 'number' && Number.isFinite(recommendation.score)\n233:       ? recommendation.score\n234:       : recommendation.confidence,\n235:     laneContributions: [],\n236:     dominantLane: null,\n237:     lifecycleStatus: 'active',\n238:     ...(Array.isArray(recommendation.ambiguousWith) ? { ambiguousWith: recommendation.ambiguousWith } : {}),\n239:     ...(typeof recommendation.heldBelow === 'string' ? { heldBelow: recommendation.heldBelow } : {}),\n240:   };\n241: }\n242: \n243: /**\n244:  * Detect whether the renderable recommendation set carries ambiguity evidence.\n245:  *\n246:  * `precomputedAmbiguous` carries the scorer's own verdict. It wins when defined: the\n247:  * scorer knows which skills a typed command held below the top and which only cleared\n248:  * a confidence floor, and serialized recommendations lose that context. Only when the\n249:  * caller has no verdict is ambiguity re-derived from the rendered fields.\n250:  */\n251: export function hasAdvisorAmbiguitySignal(\n252:   recommendations: readonly AdvisorRecommendation[],\n253:   precomputedAmbiguous?: boolean,\n254: ): boolean {\n255:   if (typeof precomputedAmbiguous === 'boolean') {\n256:     return precomputedAmbiguous;\n257:   }\n258:   return isAmbiguousTopTwo((recommendations as readonly RenderableRecommendation[]).map(toScoredRecommendation));\n259: }\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 260]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts, lines 140-259\n140:   return Math.min(Math.max(1, Math.floor(tokenCap)), MAX_TOKEN_CAP);\n141: }\n142: \n143: function capText(text: string, tokenCap: number): string {\n144:   const charCap = tokenCap * TOKEN_TO_CHAR_ESTIMATE;\n145:   if (text.length <= charCap) {\n146:     return text;\n147:   }\n148:   const truncated = text.slice(0, Math.max(1, charCap - 3)).trimEnd();\n149:   return `${truncated}...`;\n150: }\n151: \n152: function sanitizeSkillLabel(skillLabel: string | null | undefined): string | null {\n153:   if (typeof skillLabel !== 'string') {\n154:     return null;\n155:   }\n156:   const folded = canonicalFold(skillLabel);\n157:   if (/[\\n\\r]/.test(folded)) {\n158:     return null;\n159:   }\n160:   const singleLine = folded\n161:     .replace(CONTROL_CHAR_PATTERN, '')\n162:     .replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')\n163:     .trim();\n164:   if (!singleLine || INSTRUCTION_LABEL_PATTERN.test(singleLine)) {\n165:     return null;\n166:   }\n167:   return singleLine;\n168: }\n169: \n170: const DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX = 'command-doctor-';\n171: \n172: function isDoctorBridgeId(skillId: string): boolean {\n173:   return skillId.startsWith(DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX);\n174: }\n175: \n176: /** Return the sanitized runnable command for a doctor bridge id, or null when unmapped. */\n177: export function doctorCommandString(skillId: string): string | null {\n178:   if (!isDoctorBridgeId(skillId)) {\n179:     return null;\n180:   }\n181:   const command = commandRowFor(skillId)?.command;\n182:   return command === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(command);\n183: }\n184: \n185: // A recommendation that names a command renders as the skill that owns it, the\n186: // runnable command and the policy that governs the run. The recommendation's own\n187: // fields stay authoritative and the generated row fills only what they omit, so a\n188: // caller that already resolved the command is never second-guessed.\n189: function commandLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation): string | null {\n190:   const row = commandRowFor(recommendation.skill);\n191:   const command = recommendation.command ?? row?.command;\n192:   const owner = recommendation.ownerSkillId ?? row?.ownerSkillId ?? recommendation.skill;\n193:   const policy = recommendation.policy ?? row?.policy;\n194:   const commandPart = command === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(command);\n195:   const ownerPart = sanitizeSkillLabel(owner);\n196:   if (!commandPart || !ownerPart) {\n197:     return null;\n198:   }\n199:   const policyPart = policy === undefined ? null : sanitizeSkillLabel(policy);\n200:   return policyPart === null\n201:     ? `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart}`\n202:     : `${ownerPart} → ${commandPart} (${policyPart})`;\n203: }\n204: \n205: // A doctor bridge renders as its runnable command and never as its raw id; an\n206: // unmapped doctor id renders nothing.\n207: function recommendationLabel(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation): string | null {\n208:   return commandLabel(recommendation)\n209:     ?? (isDoctorBridgeId(recommendation.skill)\n210:       ? doctorCommandString(recommendation.skill)\n211:       : sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill));\n212: }\n213: \n214: function formatScore(value: number): string {\n215:   return Number.isFinite(value) ? value.toFixed(2) : '0.00';\n216: }\n217: \n218: type RenderableRecommendation = AdvisorRecommendation & {\n219:   readonly score?: number;\n220:   readonly ambiguousWith?: readonly string[];\n221:   readonly heldBelow?: string;\n222: };\n223: \n224: function toScoredRecommendation(recommendation: RenderableRecommendation): AdvisorScoredRecommendation {\n225:   return {\n226:     skill: recommendation.skill,\n227:     kind: recommendation.kind === 'command' ? 'command' : 'skill',\n228:     confidence: recommendation.confidence,\n229:     uncertainty: recommendation.uncertainty,\n230:     passes_threshold: recommendation.passes_threshold ?? true,\n231:     reason: '',\n232:     score: typeof recommendation.score === 'number' && Number.isFinite(recommendation.score)\n233:       ? recommendation.score\n234:       : recommendation.confidence,\n235:     laneContributions: [],\n236:     dominantLane: null,\n237:     lifecycleStatus: 'active',\n238:     ...(Array.isArray(recommendation.ambiguousWith) ? { ambiguousWith: recommendation.ambiguousWith } : {}),\n239:     ...(typeof recommendation.heldBelow === 'string' ? { heldBelow: recommendation.heldBelow } : {}),\n240:   };\n241: }\n242: \n243: /**\n244:  * Detect whether the renderable recommendation set carries ambiguity evidence.\n245:  *\n246:  * `precomputedAmbiguous` carries the scorer's own verdict. It wins when defined: the\n247:  * scorer knows which skills a typed command held below the top and which only cleared\n248:  * a confidence floor, and serialized recommendations lose that context. Only when the\n249:  * caller has no verdict is ambiguity re-derived from the rendered fields.\n250:  */\n251: export function hasAdvisorAmbiguitySignal(\n252:   recommendations: readonly AdvisorRecommendation[],\n253:   precomputedAmbiguous?: boolean,\n254: ): boolean {\n255:   if (typeof precomputedAmbiguous === 'boolean') {\n256:     return precomputedAmbiguous;\n257:   }\n258:   return isAmbiguousTopTwo((recommendations as readonly RenderableRecommendation[]).map(toScoredRecommendation));\n259: }\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 260]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":120}"},"time":{"start":179452